==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|processioun}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|pourciession|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|processio||a marching forward, an advance, in Late Latin a religious procession}}, from {{term|procedere}}, past participle {{term|processus||to move forward, advance, proceed}}; see [[proceed]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-procession.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[progressing]] or [[proceeding]]
# A [[group]] of people or things moving along in an [[orderly]] manner, especially if doing so [[slowly]] and [[formally]]
# A number of things [[happening]] in [[sequence]] (in [[space]] or in [[time]])

